{"title":"2025 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Why_each_row_is_twice_the_previous_row\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Why each row is twice the previous row</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(BRUTE_FORCE!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (BRUTE FORCE!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Fast)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Fast)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Cheese,_Gamble)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Cheese, Gamble)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(experience)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (experience)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Generating_Function_and_Combinatorics)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Generating Function and Combinatorics)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:50)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:50)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Quick_and_Simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Quick and Simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A Pascal-like triangle has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> as the top row and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> followed by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as the second row. In each subsequent row the first number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the last number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and, as in the standard Pascal Triangle, each other in the row is the sum of the two numbers directly above it. The first four rows are shown below.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/a/ffa2a1e4baaccc510d2f15a6267eaaa449675103.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\large{10}\\]\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/2/a5263954bc2abee88659cc71799a662888c2204d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\large{10}\\qquad\\large{1}\\]\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/d/bfd8d80b8033155a2ae20779dfade32779c7313e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\large{10}\\qquad\\large{11}\\qquad\\large{1}\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"12\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/e/64e8fc2b448fead007072cc4b3e962ea80108bd7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\large{10}\\qquad\\large{21}\\qquad\\large{12}\\qquad\\large{1}\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"12\" />\nWhat is the sum of the digits of the sum of the numbers in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />th row? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/6/9b6c8db211602f601bb90ae8187b1698eb7726f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 11 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 13 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 14 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 16 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"401\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we find the sum for each rows (I'll only do the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to illustrate the pattern), we find that row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d111a5e00ee5ea6700bb629994dc629874c505b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b45828f292e161290be6ee62bc4c9df081ee1e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/d/40d924a5d0ade21a3824a7f0343f8beae70ef96e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$88$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />. So we can see that, excluding the first row, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th row has sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/6/05680c0447ec134904a0153d61b80ec0a316da7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 \\cdot 2^{n-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"17\" />. This means the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />th row will have sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc8a87056dc76db1127abda88af42473454731f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 \\cdot 2^9 = 11 \\cdot 512 = 5632$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"193\" height=\"17\" />. The sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/1/e210a1c5ba11af200a6943e6eded6f2d47ddd152.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5632$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/6/ad6f66809be1add52e351bd651aedb1ad340b95d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~ToxicWaste\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Why_each_row_is_twice_the_previous_row\">Why each row is twice the previous row</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Why each row is twice the previous row\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Notice that the sum of each row is the slightly different than the normal Pascal's triangle, so the sum of the numbers is similar. Here's a proof of why each number in the normal Pascal's triangle is twice the previous number.\nTo prove that the sum of each row is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times the previous row, use the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/c/8cca2f2c517603930546b2f63096ba05798bf633.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${(1+1)}^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"21\" /> with the normal Pascal's triangle and use the binomial theorem from there.\n</p><p>Example: In the fifth row of Pascal's triangle, the numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/c/58c8d9ec3a1bb3ec354aa8f9c3fcb57bf4d8c91d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 4, 6, 4, 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />. The first number can be represented by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/8/908b2a93d0cd26fc1c4844753ef86eb344095a16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${4 \\choose 0} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"72\" height=\"55\" />, the second by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/4/764fd3b4d1a5873713c47ca8cc7dcb7e3d807199.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${4 \\choose 1} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"72\" height=\"55\" />, the third by  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/f/b5f3803bb802b59969d7e135f0235385427bfc79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${4 \\choose 2} = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"70\" height=\"53\" />, the fourth by  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/4/2441cfed3aabb8f7cc296975bdf9515cbd4bcf59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${4 \\choose 3} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"72\" height=\"55\" />, and the last by  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22bbda4d95463fb476c1d7f3a3377e08c7c21c2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${4 \\choose 4} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"72\" height=\"55\" />. The sum of these five numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> which is also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/f/76f27f2c52b67bb6e79df962a3defaf8c8af904b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" />. \nUsing the binomial theorem with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/6/846fa3f0c87484263c4dd57c20a2b9726fb0e300.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${(1+1)}^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"23\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/c/f4cbab0e3b88484e303914ad1d5730f82d7bc10b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 4 + 6 + 4 + 1 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"179\" height=\"15\" />, the same results in Pascal's triangle. We could also solve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/6/846fa3f0c87484263c4dd57c20a2b9726fb0e300.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${(1+1)}^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"23\" /> by converting it to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/2/9521a8469412ce4dd8556ba0edd5af8a8b1ac754.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^4 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />, proving the identity that all rows in Pascal's triangle are exactly twice the previous row and can be represented by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/550751abd3c98c2c27e593dd4a72281cea58e470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n}$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>~Bros1 (original writer of this on AMC 10A #19)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In this Pascal's Triangle-like sequence, after row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, each number in row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> appears twice in the sum of row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/cccb103143393c0119f5ab61d6d53a852ce70fcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />. For example (to illustrate the pattern), the numbers in row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and these numbers indeed each appear twice in the sum of the next row (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a10645a83b87768e7a95706c91d0a4664ca5ad2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10, 10+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are the numbers in row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so their sum can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/9/1a9b3e588a39b88f2772d94fc829ac5b987e928d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\cdot 2 + 1 \\cdot 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />). With this pattern, we know that after row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> the sum of the numbers doubles in each subsequent row, so now by the same calculation as in Solution 1, the sum of the numbers in row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5ba456de4e0130d6d4f3b4aff369b4ac42b09a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(10+1) \\cdot 2^{11-2} = 11 \\cdot 2^9 = 5632$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"251\" height=\"21\" />, and thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/0/f60d6a3dd9ddb4c0ba84778dd0e1869203ee2a1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+6+3+2 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"194\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Akang11\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28BRUTE_FORCE.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(BRUTE_FORCE!!!)\">Solution 3 (BRUTE FORCE!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (BRUTE FORCE!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can write out the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> rows with direct computation. Since no calculators are allowed, you will spend at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minutes on this problem, so I do not recommend this way. Here are the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> rows.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b311547de2920e9538f7dfbef236add0f216cd1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10\\]\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fda9788195e5b4883c4511ff704d47baa4adaff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10\\qquad 1\\]\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/a/aea1c63b66bc7d0db21ed5eec1ceb402d08af65b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10\\qquad 11\\qquad 1\\]\" width=\"109\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/5/53581509ff8e3215b3e2052cdabc02a25df6182d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10\\qquad 21\\qquad 12\\qquad 1\\]\" width=\"160\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/5/b85fd11a4c871b840e7576cc5d952c14cd36efb6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10\\qquad 31\\qquad 33\\qquad 13\\qquad 1\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5af11eee218f1ba848156fb1c49c085d8d40d1cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10\\qquad 41\\qquad 64\\qquad 46\\qquad 14\\qquad 1\\]\" width=\"263\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d172c83cc2b8740bcefcbfd9f89695d5b2da88.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10\\qquad 51\\qquad 105\\qquad 110\\qquad 60\\qquad 15\\qquad 1\\]\" width=\"333\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/8/6683c8c82881414e846034e423e7789e1ff2c69a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10\\qquad 61\\qquad 156\\qquad 215\\qquad 170\\qquad 75\\qquad 16\\qquad 1\\]\" width=\"393\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/a/06a4f08ef33e6dad44bc6ce1d331513e8c9d8750.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10\\qquad 71\\qquad 217\\qquad 371\\qquad 385\\qquad 245\\qquad 91\\qquad 17\\qquad 1\\]\" width=\"454\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/0/fb0777d5a3ff524a29f487afaa5323e9243f39ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10\\qquad 81\\qquad 288\\qquad 588\\qquad 756\\qquad 630\\qquad 336\\qquad 108\\qquad 18\\qquad 1\\]\" width=\"523\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/f/99fe6edf6b662546c45a835aa89378c36e0376ab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10\\qquad 91\\qquad 369\\qquad 876\\qquad 1344\\qquad 1386\\qquad 966\\qquad 444\\qquad 126\\qquad 19\\qquad 1\\]\" width=\"602\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Summing the last row gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/b/75bf52f255dc8819c18b3061df1be93e29ae81f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10+91+369+876+1344+1386+966+444+126+19+1 = 5632$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"557\" height=\"15\" />. Summing the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/1/e210a1c5ba11af200a6943e6eded6f2d47ddd152.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5632$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/c/fbc55ccfe23fb9e9c56b90aee8bbc9c968d541dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+6+3+2 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"194\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>Edit: After brute forcing two or three rows, it is clear that the sum doubles (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/c/97ca85eaee1193df2606f830ccc9d1bb29b72478.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11, 22, 44, 88, \\dotsc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"17\" />), and you can use this to find the sum of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />th row as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/5/23558e046500e40c21730dd0fb10d2116e19a052.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 \\cdot 2^{11-2} = 5632$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"134\" height=\"17\" />, which gives a digit sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/c/fbc55ccfe23fb9e9c56b90aee8bbc9c968d541dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+6+3+2 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"194\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~JerryZYang\n</p><p>~Sumeete(Small edit)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Fast.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Fast)\">Solution 4 (Fast)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Fast)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can just take the entire triangle modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, since all the answer choices have different residues modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and because a number is congruent to its digit sum modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Accordingly, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/c/c5c1543d172e4fc4e08cf2c1cf996b95ef1f6e59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" />, the triangle just becomes Pascal's triangle modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and so by the standard result for the row sums in Pascal's-like triangles, the sum of the numbers in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />th row is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/4/e64675ea9026978480c663d2ccfd4eab5c556408.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{11-1} = 1024 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"208\" height=\"21\" />. This means the only feasible answer choice is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, as it is the only one that is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/9/159f0b9fb702991516e2e5825997232a7c339ef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\pmod{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />, and so the answer is indeed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/e/48e9c0380575e64d9e217ad14f198e8096454da1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n~Storm1230323\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Cheese.2C_Gamble.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Cheese,_Gamble)\">Solution 5 (Cheese, Gamble)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Cheese, Gamble)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can start brute-forcing the first few rows and figure out the pattern that the sum of the numbers in row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/72287b09043ed45b372a517d764e12d07aff8071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/6/05680c0447ec134904a0153d61b80ec0a316da7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 \\cdot 2^{n-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"17\" />. Now we gamble on this pattern (which is mostly correct for AMC 10 problems) and plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, which results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/1/e210a1c5ba11af200a6943e6eded6f2d47ddd152.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5632$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Hence the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/8/ed8fb08c8e03314dee1362fc48509848ef4c63b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 6 + 3 + 2 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"194\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~ROGER8432V3\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28experience.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(experience)\">Solution 6 (experience)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (experience)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If you failed or sillied the AMC 10 A Question 19, then during the AMC 10 B you gained the experience to know that each row probably doubles in these Pascal-like problems, either in retrospect or during the actual AMC 10 A. \nHowever, we should probably check, in case you sillied this problem because you didn't check something stupid on the 10 A. \nIt is a good decision to check, because we realize that the first row does not conform to the doubling rule, and only the rows right after it do. \nThe rest of the solution is similar to how we solve the AMC 10 A Question 19, except less bashy because we only want the sum, not a specific number, and we are given the row number instead of the sum. \nSo, we end up getting the sum to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/1/e210a1c5ba11af200a6943e6eded6f2d47ddd152.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5632$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, and therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/e/48e9c0380575e64d9e217ad14f198e8096454da1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~vaishnav\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Generating_Function_and_Combinatorics.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Generating_Function_and_Combinatorics)\">Solution 7 (Generating Function and Combinatorics)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Generating Function and Combinatorics)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We want the sum of the digits of the sum of all entries in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />th row of this \"Pascal-ish\" triangle. We will solve this with far more modular arithmetic than required, even though everything collapses into a simple closed form.\n</p><p>Let the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />th row be indexed as row \\( n = 11 \\), with the top row being \\( n = 1 \\).\nDenote row sums by \\( S_n \\).\n</p><p>Each row begins with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and ends with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\nFor the interior entries, each behaves like a binomial coefficient, but with an appropriate shift, so the entries in row \\( n \\) looks like:\n</p><p>Row \\( n \\): \\( 10,  \\binom{n-2}{1} + 1,  \\binom{n-2}{2} + \\binom{n-2}{1}, \\dots,  \\binom{n-2}{n-2} + \\binom{n-2}{n-3}, 1 \\)\n</p><p>But this is too reasonable, so instead we use generating functions and modular arithmetic.\n</p><p>Define the polynomial for row \\( n \\):\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/8/4e863d7bd3ab5db2b38211bb0ecf28e88c289180.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P_n(x) = 10x^0 + \\sum_{k=1}^{n-2} \\left(\\binom{n-2}{k} \\cdot 10 + \\binom{n-2}{k-1}\\right) x^k + x^{n-1}.\\]\" width=\"462\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>The sum of the entire row is \\( P_n(1) \\).\nSo we compute:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/1/fa1668a39858118d7fd0f1304051638643648369.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P_n(1) = 10 + \\sum_{k=1}^{n-2} \\left( 10 \\binom{n-2}{k} + \\binom{n-2}{k-1} \\right) + 1.\\]\" width=\"380\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Break into two sums:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/c/35c1c1dbf9ad24d0e2b9b076b1788742a6873f4a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P_n(1) = 10 + 10 \\sum_{k=1}^{n-2} \\binom{n-2}{k} + \\sum_{k=1}^{n-2} \\binom{n-2}{k-1} + 1.\\]\" width=\"384\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>We know:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/9/e393ca6e4d4ddf3b6be8763174abc9a4994f72c7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{n-2} \\binom{n-2}{k} = 2^{n-2} - 1,\\]\" width=\"193\" height=\"53\" />\nsince it’s the full sum of binomial coefficients minus the \\( k=0 \\) term.\n</p><p>Also, similarly,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddc9c19d0dbabe1c7330dcb0aad040278d519a14.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{n-2} \\binom{n-2}{k-1} = \\sum_{j=0}^{n-3} \\binom{n-2}{j} = 2^{n-2} - \\binom{n-2}{n-2} = 2^{n-2} - 1.\\]\" width=\"468\" height=\"54\" />\n</p><p>So both sums are exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/0/ea0db980cfa4aa243fe726a91ca7b40b090057c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(2^{n-2} - 1\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"85\" height=\"23\" />, but we pretend otherwise and compute them modulo several numbers unnecessarily.\n</p><p>Since we need row \\( n = 11 \\), compute:\n</p><p>\\( n-2 = 9 \\).\n</p><p>We now compute powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> modulo various bases, even though we need the exact value.\n</p><p>First:\n</p><p>\\( 2^9 = 512 \\).\n</p><p>But we do:\n</p><p>\\( 2^1 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{10},  2^2 \\equiv 4,  2^3 \\equiv 8,  2^4 \\equiv 6,  2^5 \\equiv 2, \\), giving a cycle of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since \\( 9 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4} \\),\n</p><p>\\( 2^9 \\equiv 2^1 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{10} \\).\n</p><p>This tells us nothing, but we keep it.\n</p><p>Now compute the sums:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/c/50c09541e9a630110db0318f9392c27c232ba0fd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{9} \\binom{9}{k} = 2^9 - 1 = 511, \\text{ and hence also } \\sum_{k=1}^{9} \\binom{9}{k-1} = 511.\\]\" width=\"471\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Substitute everything:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/0/2d025de930a864bfa219b236607d434cc2c889a1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P_{11}(1) = 10 + 10 \\cdot 511 + 511 + 1.\\]\" width=\"256\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Compute in pieces:\n</p><p>\\( 10 \\cdot 511 = 5110 \\).\n</p><p>Then\n</p><p>\\( 10 + 5110 = 5120, 5120 + 511 = 5631, 5631 + 1 = 5632 \\).\n</p><p>So the sum of the entries in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />th row is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/c/98cb7c9d11205e93467824e27ce6f4f1a489e125.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5632.\\]\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>We need the sum of its digits:\n</p><p>\\( 5 + 6 + 3 + 2 = 16 \\).\n</p><p>Answer:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/2/ba2508d67ed206af0425159052dc7b67d2e9b5e4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 16}.\\]\" width=\"69\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~notvalid\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E0:50.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:50)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:50)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:50)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/gFNczjnj2DY\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/gFNczjnj2DY</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/s-Wimgu9wto\">https://youtu.be/s-Wimgu9wto</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Quick_and_Simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Quick_and_Simple)\">Video Solution(Quick and Simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</spa